# .trivyignore
# Suppress known false-positive or accepted-risk CVEs from Trivy scans.
# Format: one CVE-ID or GHSA-ID per line, with an optional comment explaining the exception.
#
# Example:
#   CVE-2023-12345  # false positive — not reachable in our build
#
# Keep this file lean. Every entry should be reviewed and re-evaluated each quarter.
# Reference: https://aquasecurity.github.io/trivy/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/#trivyignore
